ƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxHhttps://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/jul/19/could-ai-be-consciousƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;4mMz0hb05QiHOrOr_EYQDgnrEEWQL5_9FJ2UsEakRf0ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9https://newscable-source-broker.invalid/activitypub/actorƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;RDDQJccEvCaCiUhyf9tsqpxkn6tK_u3qoF41IviLobcƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;vUnUnEun_C-Q_KXPfLV9jedjzkUBhJ05j5sg8OomBl8ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxHhttps://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/jul/19/could-ai-be-consciousƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;8-0nVrwSJxaO-sz3LpRXbkXy6oOOeTDlIb2e6dRpmqUƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarky»<p>Experts believe itâ€™s at least possible. We urgently need a plan to navigate the ethical implications</p><p>In January, the AI company Anthropic published a <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/constitution">new constitution</a> for Claude, its most advanced large language model (LLM), which contained the comment: â€œWe are caught in a difficult position where we neither want&nbsp;to&nbsp;overstate the likelihood of Claudeâ€™s moral patienthood nor dismiss it out of hand.â€ A month later, Anthropicâ€™s CEO Dario Amodei went on a podcast and said his company couldnâ€™t rule out the possibility that Claude was conscious. Philosopher David Chalmers, who coined the phrase â€œthe hard problem of consciousnessâ€, has said there is a significant chance of conscious LLMs within a decade. And what about Claude itself? When asked during testing to estimate the probability that it&nbsp;is a <em>moral patient</em>, meaning that its wellbeing matters&nbsp;in its own right, it gave numbers ranging from 5% to 40% and stressed how uncertain it was.</p><p>Modern AI systems are extraordinarily complex, and they are advancing fast. In terms of structural complexity and computational scale, by some measures a few are already in the range of a mouse brain, and at recent growth rates, they could reach the range of a human brain within five to 10 years.</p> <a href="https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/jul/19/could-ai-be-conscious">Continue reading...</a>ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;63y8JoYJ2BIzd3wSfvuh9g-P2x_A3ex5Uw-ag_JWGoAƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;E1GosUwXKmPfcczdhWDcGGbiMlXZ7Ml3mVF0-AqGDqoƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;jAUxyqlFG6dvI13tNhjblekSxnnG8cZsRjJdYNvERR4ƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;CNEaRP8CX-ooeX53nFSqsS_QzYv_Cq3tj-Rovuz68REƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkefalseƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;gtSGDp37AmugEWvdKaJOoDEkfVb8uBecZp0HBb02hssƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkdtrueƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;b2HcytnWJqJ3ThbB-m_ksdaT6iuJiysEcEXi65iOZo0ƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;oA9-te7XhNZSnAyo48n1qg2cntYKAurr27OOXLbtDi8ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkdTextƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;eogt5pwN7gKZSMt1QBfNlmcQJyQleniaTYXfRVDvPhEƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkqSyndicationSourceƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;B8YvegSpDT0